cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use ValleScope in your research, please cite it using the following metadata.
title: "ValleScope: Context-based correspondence assignment for satellite DNA in telomere-to-telomere assemblies"
version: "0.1.0"
doi: "DOI"
date-released: 2026-5-15
authors:
  - family-names: "Hiura"
    given-names: "Nobuhiro"
    github: "https://github.com/hiura-censat"
    affiliation: "Graduate School of Medical and Dental Sciences, Institute of Science Tokyo"

abstract: >
ValleScope is a framework for assigning high-confidence assembly-to-assembly correspondences in highly repetitive arrays, including centromeric and pericentromeric α-satellite and HSat2. ValleScope does not aim to maximize continuous alignment coverage. Instead, it defines high-confidence correspondence blocks using tokenized structural contexts, and context-based assignment algorithm. The resulting ValleScope-defiened correspondence intervals can be used for comparative analysis of satellite DNA structural variation and haplotype diversity.
repository-code: "https://github.com/hiura-censat/ValleScope"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - satellite DNA
  - centromere
  - pericentromere
  - α-satellite
  - HSat2
  - genomics
  - T2T
  - assembly-to-assembly

